# Frequently asked questions

## Do agents run in Pontia Cloud?

No. Agent Clients, tools, credentials, and project files stay on your device. Pontia Cloud coordinates identity and remote authorization; an Edge relays encrypted traffic.

## Is a Workspace an operating-system sandbox?

No. Workspace roots limit what the Pontia browser exposes for activation and file discovery. The Agent Client still has the permissions and sandbox policy of its local process.

## Can I use Pontia without an account?

Yes. The local Dashboard uses an External API token and listens on the device's loopback address; access from elsewhere requires a secure tunnel or forwarding configuration. The hosted Remote Dashboard requires a Pontia Cloud login and registered device.

## Can Pontia read my prompts or project data?

Pontia has three runtime components:

- **Pontia Cloud** manages users, authentication, device registration, and access authorization. It does not receive Dashboard traffic or project files.
- **pontiad** runs on your device, coordinates Agent Clients, and serves prompts and agent data to your Dashboard.
- **Pontia Edge** relays end-to-end encrypted traffic between the browser and `pontiad`. It cannot decrypt that traffic.

Your prompts and project data remain on your device.

## What should I back up?

Back up project files independently. `$PONTIA_HOME` contains local control state, Workflow files, and sensitive credentials; back it up only to a trusted encrypted destination. Agent Client native conversation data may live outside `PONTIA_HOME` and follows that Client's own backup rules.

## Does Pontia support Windows?

No. The local control plane supports Linux and macOS 11 or later. Self-hosted Edge supports Linux only.
